 ## Overview
-Area-Averaged Resampling is a downsampling technique that computes the average color of an input image region mapped to a single output pixel, weighted by the area of overlap between the input pixel grid and the mapped output pixel region [S1, unofficial]. It differs from nearest-neighbor or simple box filtering by explicitly calculating the geometric intersection area between the continuous output pixel footprint and the discrete input pixel grid [S1, unofficial].
